{
  "esm": "0.6.0",
  "metadata": {
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciDiscretizations/gastown.furiosa"
    ],
    "description": "DUO edge + MPAS Voronoi-dual GEOMETRY expressed as a semiring-FAQ value-invention pass (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir \u00a78.1 geometry FAQ; bead esd-heg.7 / D2b), the declarative replacement for the geometry half of the imperative _duo_voronoi_dual (src/grids/mpas.jl, steps 1 / circumcenters / 5 / area) and the DUO Tier-U edge_length / cell_distance accessors (src/grids/duo.jl), plus their per-binding equivalents. The COMPANION of voronoi_dual_topology.esm (D1b, esd-heg.2): that document produces the dual topology (cells_on_cell / edges_on_cell) and the angularly-ordered incident-face ring (sorted_vertex_faces); this one consumes that ring (ring_face / ring_face_next) for the dual-cell area fan and produces every dual geometric metric. Inputs (CONST, supplied by the topology/geometry passes): vert_coord (MPAS cell = DUO vertex unit direction = duo.vertices/R), centroid (DUO face centroid = D2a cell_cart/R), face_vert / edge_cell / edge_face / ring_face connectivity, and R. Outputs: (1) circumcenter (circ_x/y/z) \u2014 the DUO face circumcenter (MPAS dual vertex) as the normalized cross-product sum a\u00d7b+b\u00d7c+c\u00d7a; the imperative outward-orientation flip (cc\u00b7centroid<0 \u2192 negate, which fires for EVERY face on the consistently-wound icosahedral mesh) is reproduced bit-for-bit as the standard cross sum NEGATED (\u00d7\u22121.0), so no data-dependent branch is needed and even zero components keep the imperative's \u22120.0 (reversing the operand order would not: x\u2212x is +0.0 reversed but \u22120.0 negated). (2) dc_edge \u2014 cell-center-to-cell-center great-circle arc R\u00b7acos(\u00b7), identical to the DUO edge_length (vertex-to-vertex arc). (3) dv_edge \u2014 Voronoi-vertex-to-vertex arc R\u00b7acos(\u00b7) over the two incident circumcenters. (4) cell_distance \u2014 the DUO Tier-U centroid-to-centroid arc (distinct from dv_edge, which uses circumcenters). (5) lon_cell / lat_cell \u2014 MPAS cell-centre geographic coords. (6) lon_edge / lat_edge \u2014 geographic coords of the normalized edge midpoint. (7) area_cell \u2014 the Voronoi dual-cell area as the spherical-excess (L'Huilier) FAN from the cell centre over consecutive circumcenter pairs in the D1b angular ring, summed and scaled by R\u00b2. Squares are products (not ^), reductions and tan-products are folded in space/ring order, and the cross sum is standard-order-negated \u2014 so the FAQ reproduces the imperative float ops bit-for-bit; deterministic formulas with NO clipping (clamp/max), per the acceptance contract: on a valid icosahedral mesh every acos argument and the L'Huilier radicand already lie in range, so clipping never fires and the bytes match. Value-free structural spec (connectivity/coords are parameter shapes; concrete data fed by the conformance harness). Index sizes are the canonical level-0 dual instance (the icosahedron\u2192dodecahedron dual: cells=12 pentagons, faces=20, edges=30, ring=5); the pass shape is identical at any level (the ring becomes ragged 5/6 once subdivision introduces hexagons). Byte/numeric equivalence to _duo_voronoi_dual and edge_length / cell_distance is proven across dual levels 1/2/3 by test/test_duo_edge_dual_geometry_faq.jl.",
    "name": "duo_edge_dual_geometry",
    "tags": [
      "duo",
      "mpas",
      "icosahedral",
      "voronoi-dual",
      "geometry",
      "circumcenter",
      "cross-product",
      "dc-edge",
